AU  - Vincent, O. R.; Folorunso, Olusegun
TI  - A Descriptive Algorithm for Sobel Image Edge Detection
PY  - 2009
AB  - Image edge detection is a process of locating the e dge of an image which is important in finding the approximate absolute gradient magnitude at each point I of an input grayscale image. The problem of getting an appropriate absolute gradient magnitude for edges lies in the method used. The Sobel operator performs a 2-D spatial gradient measurement on images. Transferring a 2-D pixel array into statistically uncorrelated data se t enhances the removal of redundant data, as a result, reduction of the amount of data is required to represent a digital image. The Sobel edge detector uses a pair of 3 x 3 convolution masks, one estimating gradient in the x-direction and the other estimating gradient in y‐direction. The Sobel detector is incredibly sensit ive to noise in pictures, it effectively highlight them as edges. Henc e, Sobel operator is recommended in massive data communication found in data transfer.
