AB  - Fertilization in mammalian and nonmammalian organisms has many features in common. These features include a final maturation phase for sperm and eggs, species-specific binding of sperm to eggs, penetration by sperm of one or more extracellular coats surrounding eggs, fusion of sperm and eggs, and activation of eggs. Implicit in this are a variety of basic molecular events, including receptor-ligand interactions, signalling cascades, specific proteolysis, and nuclear transformations. Here, several of these events are addressed for fertilization in animals as diverse as starfish and mice.
