AU  - Liu, Zixuan; Li, Fang; Hou, Linjing; Shi, Yuhang
TI  - Multi-Object Tracking Algorithm Based on Improved ByteTrack
PY  - 2024
AB  - With the rapid advancements of computer vision technology, the application of multi-object tracking in complex scenes is receiving increasing attention. For example, occlusion and appearance changes in complex scenes, target confusion and ID switching in densely populated environments, and adaptability to different environments. To alleviate the problem of poor tracking performance caused by missed detections, Re-ID appearance features are added to the first matching of ByteTrack, and DIoU is used to replace the original IoU matching in the second matching of ByteTrack. To improve the boundary box drift caused by Kalman filtering during camera motion, Global Motion Compensation technology is used to address the issue of motion camera jitter, while also alleviating the problems of target occlusion and motion nonlinearity. The effectiveness and superiority of this approach have been further validated through additional assessment metrics and ablation studies.
