AU  - Roobini, M.S.; Rishikesh, P.; Avinash, P.; Rayen, Sonia Jenifer; Clarinda, Scinthia
TI  - Classifying the Problem of Infertility using Image Processing Techniques with Neural Networks
PY  - 2025
AB  - Infertility is a global health issue affecting millions, with significant challenges in accurate diagnosis and treatment. This paper explores using various texts for processing images integrated with neural networks for classifying infertility-related conditions. By leveraging Techniques like image segmentation, feature extraction, and advanced methods such as deep learning models, especially convolutional neural networks (CNNs), are widely utilized. The proposed system analyzes medical images like ultrasounds and MRIs to identify abnormalities such as ovarian cysts, endometriosis, and uterine fibroids. The study emphasizes the effectiveness of preprocessing methods to enhance image quality and reduce noise, as well as advanced neural network architectures for robust feature extraction and classification. Experimental results demonstrate improved diagnostic accuracy, offering a non-invasive and efficient tool for medical professionals. This approach holds potential to transform infertility diagnostics, providing reliable support for clinical decision-making while addressing privacy and ethical concerns associated with AI in healthcare.
