AU  - Jayakrishna, S.S; Sankar Ganesh, S
TI  - An Enhanced Deep-Learning-Based Workflow For Detection of Banana Leaf Stomata From Brightfield Microscopic Images
PY  - 2024
AB  - Stomata are vital in plants as they regulate water exchange, control the rate of transpiration, and aid photosynthesis for a sustainable ecological carbon cycle. An automated workflow for detecting stomata has been developed to locate their region in banana leaves. To create our digital image dataset, we collected banana leaf samples from farmers’ fields. After preprocessing the images, we manually annotated them and sent them for training. The custom dataset was evaluated using Detectron2, which achieved an 86.2 % mAP, 81.4 % precision, and 74.7 % recall. We compared the model’s performance with different base models and configurations, including R-CNN, RetinaNet, AlexNet, and TensorFlow object detection. and we summarize our current understanding of the topic. Our study provides a novel perspective for stomata visualization.
